      "title": "Strong oxidant, no lasting residual",
      "description": "Ozone is a very strong oxidant: it disinfects (including Cryptosporidium at higher C·t), removes colour, taste and odour, and oxidises iron, manganese and micro-pollutants. It is made on site because it decomposes quickly. Transfer into water depends on bubble size and contact depth; leftover ozone in the off-gas is destroyed before venting because it is toxic (workplace limits ~ 0.1 ppm).",
